-- Karta Wedkarska (27620) is what CHARACTER::fishing() wants worn, and the
-- package sells it in exactly one place: the Fisherman's special shop,
-- world.shop_special 9009 - 25 000 yang and five Materialy Rzemieslnicze
-- (30378, the storekeeper's material exchange), once in twenty-two hours, and
-- from level thirty since apply.sh lowered the package's fifty to the rod's
-- own thirty (17 September); the check below says the same number so
-- the dialog does not refuse what the shop sells. Nothing in the package
-- opens that shop: special_shop.quest answers 20406, 9006 and the three
-- guards, and no quest names 9009, so no
-- player could ever buy a pass ("gdzie mozna zdobyc fishing pass?" - "Nie da
-- sie", Greess and SIZOWSKI, 17 September). This is the Fisherman's button for
-- it. The engine keeps the shop's own limits; fishing still wants the
-- Fisherman's introduction (fishing_onboarding) finished. Bots never come
-- through here - they buy theirs in the AI (EnsurePlayerBotFishingPass).
-- Polish or English as the player's client asked (playerbot_lang.quest). The
-- English says "fishing pass" and not the English locale pack's "Fishing
-- Book": every client names an item from the one gamedata item_proto, the
-- package's Polish, so that name is one nobody sees.
quest fishing_pass_shop begin
    state start begin
        function t(pl, en)
            if pc.getf("playerbot_lang", "en") == 1 then
                return en
            end
            return pl
        end

        when 9009.chat.fishing_pass_shop.t("Karta Wedkarska", "Fishing pass") begin
            if pc.get_level() < 30 then
                npc_name()
                say(fishing_pass_shop.t("Karte Wedkarska sprzedaje od 30 poziomu.", "I sell the fishing pass from level 30."))
                return
            end
            setskin(NOWINDOW)
            pc.open_special_shop(9009)
        end
    end
end
